      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "03.15.2023 Update\n\nUpdated Creator Companion to v2.0.2, problem still exists.\n\nhttps://i.imgur.com/nwaAvBu.mp4\n\nAn option to have the ability to turn off the graph auto scrolling would remedy this situation. Please consider this addition, as this makes working within the graph physically impossible for me.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-08T14:59:10.244Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The exact reasoning behind this request, as well as photos and videos detailing the issue, can be found in my \"UDON VR\" Discord post: https://discord.com/channels/706637693693722715/1082743786150568057\n\nLong and short of the request is this, because of the auto-scrolling in the UDON Graph, when ever I create two NODES, and try to drag the one NODE close to the other NODE, the NODE that I am not pushing with the mouse, runs away from the NODE that I am moving via the mouse. Even with my Windows resolution scale size at 100%, this issue remains. And as you will see, in the Discord discussion, if I make the UDON Graph window float, and then maximize the floating window, then, this issue does not happen, but to continually do that, while programming, is beyond burdensome. As suggested to me, in the Discord discussion, I am hoping that the ability of being able to turn off auto-scrolling, as an option, would remedy this situation.",
